Create two coordinated, text-free outcome title plaques for the Urkaaaz
Victory/Defeat match-result popup.

## References

- Attach `assets_src/match/result-ui/match_result_popup_panel.png` as the
  primary reference for material, lighting, trim, and scale.
- Use `docs/systems/match-result-popup-mockup.agp` for the popup composition
  and the distinction between Victory and Defeat.
- The plaques are separate overlays on the shared panel. Do not redraw or
  replace the panel, its transparent illustration window, or its top
  level/biome plaque.

## Output

- Generate exactly two separate isolated PNG assets:
  - `match_result_victory_plaque.png`
  - `match_result_defeat_plaque.png`
- Save both under `assets_src/match/result-ui/`.
- Canvas: exactly 1920 x 480 pixels, RGBA, transparent background. This is a
  4x source for a 480 x 120 dp target.
- Center each plaque in its canvas with even transparent margins. Keep the
  complete silhouette and any soft shadow inside the canvas.
- Both plaques must have the same canvas size, silhouette footprint, visual
  weight, and alignment so Android can use them in the same position.

## Shared design

- Create one compact, horizontal title plaque that can overlap the shared
  popup panel's upper border without obscuring the level/biome plaque or
  illustration window.
- Match the shared Urkaaaz finish: dark iron or wood inset, warm bronze/gold
  edging, restrained rivets, dimensional bevels, and controlled highlights.
- Keep the center calm and wide enough for a live Android outcome label:
  `VICTORY!` or `DEFEAT`.
- Do not render any letters, words, numbers, punctuation, logos, or
  typography. Android renders localized text separately in Cinzel SemiBold.
- Keep the center surface sufficiently dark and uncluttered for pale or
  warm-gold live text to remain readable.
- Avoid thin details that disappear when scaled to 480 x 120 dp.

## Victory plaque

- Output: `match_result_victory_plaque.png`.
- Use a confident warm-gold highlight treatment that complements, but does
  not compete with, the shared popup frame.
- Optional decoration may include a restrained laurel or celebratory metal
  detail at the ends of the plaque. Keep its center clear for live text.
- The mood should feel triumphant and welcoming, not premium, magical, or
  reward-specific.

## Defeat plaque

- Output: `match_result_defeat_plaque.png`.
- Use a restrained ember-red or dark-copper accent while retaining the same
  neutral iron/wood material and overall plaque geometry as Victory.
- Optional decoration may include a subtle scuffed edge or subdued ember
  detail at the ends. Keep its center clear for live text.
- Keep the mood encouraging and readable; avoid damage that suggests injury,
  gore, or humiliation.

## Runtime separation

- These are decorative plaque backgrounds only. Do not bake in the outcome
  title, level, biome, score, reward, unlock, or button content.
- Victory and Defeat use their respective plaque PNGs, while the shared panel
  and all other popup controls remain separate runtime layers.
- Do not include a character, catapult, battlefield, landscape, or illustration
  in either plaque; those belong in separate artwork.
- Do not add a gold-reward or progression claim to either design.

## Negative prompt

text, letters, words, numbers, punctuation, logo, watermark, signature,
button, button label, reward, coin, unlock, character, unit, catapult,
battlefield, landscape, illustration, full popup panel, opaque canvas,
cropped plaque, clipped bevel, oversized laurels, aggressive flames, gore,
injury, humiliating imagery, excessive glow, tiny unreadable detail

## Review checklist

- Confirm exactly two PNGs exist with the requested names and dimensions.
- Confirm both use RGBA and transparent pixels outside the plaque silhouette.
- Confirm the plaque silhouettes have matching size, shape, and alignment.
- Confirm the center of each plaque is clear for live Cinzel SemiBold text.
- Confirm Victory is warm gold and Defeat is restrained ember-red/copper.
- Preview both at 480 x 120 dp over the shared popup panel.
- Do not import these assets into Android or change runtime layout until both
  are reviewed and approved.
